        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ruxton Park, Manitou Springs, El Paso County, Colorado Springs, Colorado\n- Parks and Mountains: Ruxton Park, Pikes Peak, Pike National Forest\n- Concepts: elevation, ultra-prominent fourteener, location bearings\n\nFacts:\n- Ruxton Park is a park in Manitou Springs, El Paso County, Colorado.\n- Ruxton Park has an elevation of 9,078 feet.\n- Pikes Peak is an ultra-prominent fourteener with an elevation of 4,302.31 meters.\n- Pikes Peak is located in Pike National Forest.\n- Pikes Peak is 19.3 kilometers west by south, at a bearing of 263 degrees, from downtown Colorado Springs, Colorado.",
